Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.07,0:00:00.83,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}In this town,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.83,0:00:02.10,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}a giant die rolls
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.10,0:00:02.97,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}every sunrise.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.97,0:00:04.92,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Today, it landed on three.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.63,0:00:06.71,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}All across the plaza,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.71,0:00:08.23,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}people rose off the ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.23,0:00:09.63,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}A baker grabbed his stall
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.63,0:00:10.90,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}as his shoes floated away.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.23,0:00:11.84,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Everyone was rising.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.84,0:00:12.29,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Except Leo.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.73,0:00:14.02,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}He'd tied himself
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.02,0:00:14.98,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}to the clock tower.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.98,0:00:16.47,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Leo hated surprises.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.47,0:00:17.92,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}He even kept a notebook
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.92,0:00:18.84,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}listing what to do
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.84,0:00:19.84,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}if the town suddenly
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.84,0:00:20.55,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}lost gravity.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.03,0:00:22.02,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Every roll changed the law.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.02,0:00:23.37,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}One floated loose objects.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.37,0:00:24.03,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Two made everyone
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.03,0:00:24.87,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}walk backward.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.87,0:00:25.59,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Three lifted people
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.59,0:00:26.13,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}into the air.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.46,0:00:27.42,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}But in thirty years,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.42,0:00:28.64,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the die had never
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.64,0:00:29.36,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}landed on six.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.55,0:00:30.76,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Leo had counted the rolls.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.76,0:00:31.93,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}And he'd noticed
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.93,0:00:33.08,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}something strange:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.08,0:00:33.65,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}whenever six
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.65,0:00:34.45,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}almost appeared,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.45,0:00:35.38,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the die made
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.38,0:00:36.43,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the exact same wobble.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.63,0:00:37.40,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}So while the town
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.40,0:00:38.22,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}floated above him,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.22,0:00:39.59,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Leo slipped underneath
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.59,0:00:40.45,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the stone platform.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.68,0:00:41.68,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}There was a brass
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.68,0:00:43.19,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}paddle and a crank.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.19,0:00:44.20,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Somebody had been
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.20,0:00:45.49,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}knocking the die
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.49,0:00:46.65,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}away from six before
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.65,0:00:47.61,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}it could settle.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.06,0:00:48.93,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Mayor Pip was holding
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.93,0:00:49.45,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the handle.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.84,0:00:50.81,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Pip looked ten,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.81,0:00:51.96,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}but he'd started the game
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.96,0:00:53.05,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}thirty years earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.05,0:00:54.00,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Nobody inside
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.00,0:00:55.00,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the town grew older.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.00,0:00:56.59,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Outside, his family had.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.01,0:00:57.42,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Pip held
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.42,0:00:58.93,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}their faded photograph.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.93,0:00:59.54,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}“If six lands,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.54,0:01:00.47,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the gate opens,”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.47,0:01:01.05,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}he whispered.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.05,0:01:02.42,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}“What if they've
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.42,0:01:03.50,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}forgotten me?”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.50,0:01:04.25,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Leo had an answer
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.25,0:01:05.38,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}for almost everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.38,0:01:06.15,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}But not that.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.57,0:01:07.30,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}He pulled a small
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.30,0:01:08.26,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}pin from the machine,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.26,0:01:09.22,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}stopping the paddle,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.22,0:01:10.96,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}and placed it in Pip's hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.96,0:01:11.88,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}“You can put it back,”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.88,0:01:12.68,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Leo said.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.68,0:01:14.13,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}“I won't stop you.”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.13,0:01:14.84,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}The next morning,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.84,0:01:16.58,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the die didn't land on six.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.58,0:01:17.57,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Neither did the next.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.00,0:01:18.96,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Five mornings went by.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.96,0:01:20.31,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Pip watched each roll,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.31,0:01:21.21,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}holding the pin.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.21,0:01:22.97,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Once, he almost returned it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.97,0:01:23.97,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Then he looked
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.97,0:01:24.96,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}at the photograph
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.96,0:01:25.71,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}and put it down.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.18,0:01:27.50,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}On the sixth sunrise,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.50,0:01:28.65,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the die began to turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.97,0:01:30.17,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}It rocked toward six.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.53,0:01:31.62,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Pip reached for the pin,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.62,0:01:32.90,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}and stopped himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.90,0:01:34.58,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}The die settled.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.00,0:01:36.60,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Six.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.60,0:01:37.93,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}The town gate swung open.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.93,0:01:38.88,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Pip ran through it,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.88,0:01:39.48,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}past streets
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.48,0:01:41.03,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}he barely recognized,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.03,0:01:41.92,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}until he reached
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.92,0:01:43.00,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}his old house.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.00,0:01:44.10,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}An older woman stood
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.10,0:01:45.00,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}in the doorway.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.00,0:01:46.41,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}She took one look at him
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.41,0:01:47.31,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}and said his name.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.66,0:01:48.47,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Inside was a small chair
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.47,0:01:49.32,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}by the kitchen table.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.32,0:01:50.54,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Everything had changed
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.54,0:01:51.46,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}except that chair.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.46,0:01:52.46,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}“We kept your chair,”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.46,0:01:52.91,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}she said.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.98,0:01:53.37,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}And Leo,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.37,0:01:54.79,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}watching from the open gate,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.79,0:01:55.87,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}finally closed his notebook
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.87,0:01:56.92,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}without planning tomorrow.
